body:
Integrated ee60a22. Students' private questions (S15 private_questions placement) are rows in public.questions with owner_user_id set and status 'published'.
New guard apps/api/tests/test_question_scope.py: every SQL statement that touches public.questions must do one of:
(a) filter on the questions row's own owner_user_id: 'owner_user_id is null' for shared/admin/authoring paths, or '(q.owner_user_id is null or q.owner_user_id = <caller>)' for a student acting through the pool;
(b) sit under a '# questions-scope: rls|insert|id-unique|seed|write-only (<why>)' comment.
I edited files owned by:
- seg19: admin/questions.py, coverage.py, chapters.py, reports.py, sibling_queues.py;
- seg21: authoring/review_store.py, routes.py, store.py, psychometrics_job.py;
- seg14: assistant/questions.py;
- S08/S09: qbank/routes.py, exam.py, exam_routes.py;
- seg10: cards/routes.py;
- seg16: plan/routes.py;
- others: courses, notes, ink, embeddings/query, analytics, seed/importer (scope comments only).
Behaviour change: an admin GET /api/admin/questions/<private id> is a 404, and private rows never appear in lists, queues, coverage or psychometrics. db test: tests/ingest/test_private_questions_db.py. Please rebase; a new query on questions needs (a) or (b).
